[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,4.0);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (3.4,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:2.8,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.45*\x*\x});
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.6,2.0) {Distance from driveway top};
\node[font=\small] at (1.7,-0.6) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Theo starts skateboarding down his driveway, gradually building up speed.
The graph shows his distance from the top of the driveway.
Which statement correctly describes his motion?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,3.4);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (3.6,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:3.0,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{-0.3*(\x-3.0)*(\x-3.0)+2.7});
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.6,1.7) {Distance from tent};
\node[font=\small] at (1.8,-0.6) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Layla walks away from her tent along a track, quickly at first and then more gradually.
The graph shows her distance from the tent.
Which statement correctly describes her motion?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,3.2);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (3.6,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:3.0,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2.7-0.3*\x*\x});
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.6,1.6) {Distance from lodge};
\node[font=\small] at (1.8,-0.6) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Marco skis back down towards the lodge after reaching the top of the run.
The graph shows his distance from the lodge.
Which statement correctly describes his motion?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,3.6);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (3.8,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:3.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3.2*exp(-0.85*\x)});
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.6,1.8) {Distance from owner};
\node[font=\small] at (1.9,-0.6) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A dog runs back towards its owner, fast at first and then slowing as it gets close.
The graph shows the dog's distance from its owner.
Which statement correctly describes its motion?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.05]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,4.0);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (3.4,0);
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0) -- (1.4,1.4);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:1.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x+1.4},{1.4+\x+0.4*\x*\x});
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.6,1.5) {Distance travelled};
\node[font=\small] at (1.7,-0.6) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Grace jogs at an even pace, then sprints, building up further speed.
The graph shows her distance travelled.
Which statement correctly describes her motion?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,3.6);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (3.7,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:3.1,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{-0.32*(\x-3.1)*(\x-3.1)+3.0752});
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.6,1.8) {Distance from home};
\node[font=\small] at (1.85,-0.6) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Ben cycles away from home.
The graph shows his distance from home.
Which statement correctly describes his motion?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,2.4);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (5.6,0);
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0) -- (1.4,1.4);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:1.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x+1.4},{1.4+(-0.32*(\x-1.4)*(\x-1.4)+0.6272)});
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:1.6,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x+2.8},{2.0272-0.3*\x*\x});
\draw[thick,blue] (4.4,1.2592) -- (5.0,1.2592);
\node[font=\small] at (0.7,0.55) {A};
\node[font=\small] at (2.1,1.95) {B};
\node[font=\small] at (3.6,1.85) {C};
\node[font=\small] at (4.7,1.45) {D};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.6,1.2) {Distance from home};
\node[font=\small] at (2.8,-0.6) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The graph shows a walker's distance from home over four labelled stages.
During which stage is the walker speeding up?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.95]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,3.0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(3.0,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:2.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2.6-0.4*\x*\x});
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.5,1.5) {Distance from home};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (1.5,-0.5) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Ana walks along a straight path.
Which statement correctly describes her distance from home and her speed?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,3.5);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.7,0);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:1.4,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.5*\x*\x});
\draw[thick,blue] (1.4,0.98)--(2.4,2.38);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:1.0,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x+2.4},{2.38+0.7*(2*\x-\x*\x)});
\draw[thick,blue] (3.4,3.08)--(4.0,3.08);
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:1.2,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x+4.0},{3.08-0.6*\x*\x});
\node[font=\small] at (0.8,0.65) {A};
\node[font=\small] at (1.9,1.35) {B};
\node[font=\small] at (2.9,2.55) {C};
\node[font=\small] at (3.7,2.8) {D};
\node[font=\small] at (4.7,2.9) {E};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-0.6,1.75) {Distance from home};
\node[font=\small] at (2.85,-0.6) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Priya walks along a straight path.
Which description correctly gives her motion during stages C, D and E, in that order?
